# rtl8xxxu on the RTOS line, the AP role (A1-A3): the RTL8188EUS becomes a
# 2.4 GHz AP (SSID rtos-8188-ap, ch5/2432, HT20, open), the Pi's MT7921AU joins
# it, and the data plane is proven both ways.
#
# The AP MLME is the imported NXP hostapd (CONFIG_HOSTAP_AP); mac80211 keeps the
# AP state machine and rtl8xxxu sends the beacon from the host
# (update_beacon_work -> rtl8xxxu_send_beacon_frame, TX queue BEACON) - the
# first host-sent beacon on this line, unlike the rtw88/rtw89 arms' firmware
# beacons.  The station's own C5 ladder is not this image: the card is beaconing
# a BSS, not joining one.
#
# The driver carries two recorded patches for this role (wireless-drivers/
# rtl8xxxu/patches/): the 8188e fileops' supports_ap/max_macid_num enablement
# and the station macid in the v3 TX descriptor.  Mainline has no AP mode for
# this chip; both patches come from the pending upstream series and its review.
#
# What this profile is not: the phase table (a throughput verdict needs its own
# pre-registration), WPA2, 5 GHz, monitor, and the station role.
#
# The driver + stack are a GPL-2.0 link product; the imported hostapd is
# BSD-3-Clause and the rtl8188eu firmware is redistributed with the image
# (docs/LICENSES.md).

CONFIG_BACKEND_FREERTOS=y
CONFIG_OPT_O2=y
CONFIG_PROFILE_BASE=y
CONFIG_HEAP_SIZE=16
CONFIG_CASES="tick rtl8xxxu_ap"
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_PCI=n
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_SDIO=n
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_USB=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_WIRELESS=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_RTL8XXXU=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_NET_LWIP=y
CONFIG_HOSTAP_AP=y
CONFIG_FREERTOS_HEAP_SIZE=16777216
CONFIG_LKPI_USB_CHERRYUSB_STAGE_SIZE=32768
CONFIG_LKPI_USB_CHERRYUSB_STAGE_SLOTS=16
CONFIG_RUNNER_STACK_KB=32
CONFIG_RTL8XXXU_USB_BUS=0
